"F4 fixture: one constraint touches BOTH a DENSE block and a SPARSE block (m=18)."
"   blockStruct = [2, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3]: block 1 is 2x2, blocks 2..7 are 3x3."
"   Constraint 1 carries E11 in the 2x2 block 1 (1 nonzero / 4 entries = 25%"
"   > 20% density gate -> :dense) AND E11 in the sparse 3x3 block 2 (11% ->"
"   :sparse). The sparse block selects F3 for constraint 1 (f3 < f1, f2 with"
"   inz=1, up=1), while the dense block must stay F1/F2. Pre-F4 the single"
"   per-constraint useFormula slot let block 2's F3 leak into block 1,"
"   tripping the _check_no_F3_on_dense! assert (or cal_f3! BoundsError)."
"   Constraints 1 and 2 cover the 2x2 block (E11, E22); constraints (1,2,3)"
"   cover block 2 (E11, E22, E33); triples (3g-2, 3g-1, 3g) cover block g"
"   for g=3..7. C = I per block, so tr(X) is fully pinned by the equality"
"   constraints (the REVERSE_PRIMAL_DUAL solve of min <-C, X> is bounded)."
"   b = [2, 2, 1, ..., 1] (constraints 1, 2 span two diagonal entries)."
"   Strictly feasible: primal X = I, dual y = (1-eps, ..., 1). Optimum: 20."
18  =  mDIM
7  =  nBLOCK
2 3 3 3 3 3 3  =  bLOCKsTRUCT
